# macOS custom-folder-icon marker files. This repo lives in a Google-Drive-synced
# folder, which keeps dropping these into every directory (including inside .git,
# where an untracked one landing in refs/ can make git misread it as a corrupt
# ref — "fatal: bad object refs/Icon?"). Keep this ignored so it's never committed
# and so `git status` doesn't get noisy; if it recurs inside .git itself, delete
# the zero-byte file directly (`find .git -iname "Icon*" -type f -size 0 -delete`).
Icon?
Icon
